infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Observer effect: which profiler perturbs least
  desc Every profiler distorts what it measures — match it to the question, keep overhead under the 5% trust line
  compares
    - label Sampling profiler
      children
        - label Sampling: periodic stack walks
          desc Snapshots the call stack on a timer, not on every call
        - label 100 Hz adds 0.5-2% overhead
          desc Under the 5% trust line — safe to run on live production traffic
        - label 1000 Hz can reach 10%
          desc Higher sample rate buys resolution but breaches the 5% budget
        - label Best for production profiling
          desc Finds the next bottleneck on real traffic at negligible cost
    - label Instrumentation profiler
      children
        - label Instrumentation: times every call
          desc Wraps each entry/exit, so it counts calls exactly
        - label 20-100% overhead in JIT runtimes
          desc Wrapping each call blocks the optimiser from inlining
        - label Exact entry/exit call counts
          desc Precise where sampling only estimates — but distorts the timings
        - label Best for tight microbenchmarks
          desc Use only where exact counts justify the heavy perturbation
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
